SHOP_IMMORTAL
SHOP_IMMORTAL
 
Immortal commands
-------------------------
 
&Wshow player_shops&n
Shows all player-owned shops, including the room number,
monthly rent, if it's active, and how many items are for sale.
 
(Note: the "where" command has been updated to include player
shops).
 
&Wshop create <player_name> <room_vnum> <rent>&n
Example: shop create Modred 3014 50000
  Creates a shop for Modred at The Marketplace in Heliopolis
  and charges his bank account 50K coins each calendar month.
 
&Wshop delete <player_name> <room_vnum>&n
Example: shop delete Modred 3014
  Deletes Modred's shop.  The shop must have no inventory for
  this to work (remove the player's items first).
 
&Wshop remove #<item_number>&n
Example: shop remove #4
  Immortals can remove objects from any player's shop (use this
  only when appropriate).  To use this command, stand in the
  player's shop.
 
&Wshop rent <player_name> <amount>&n
Example: shop rent Modred 100000
  Sets Modred's monthly rent to 100K coins.
 
&Wshop sales_tax <percent>&n
Example: shop sales_tax 10
  Sets the world-wide sales tax for purchases to 10%.
  (So If I buy something for 10 coins, the sales tax is 1 coin).
 
&Wshop active <player_name> <"true"|"false">&n
Example: shop active Modred true
  Sets Modred's shop to active.
When a shop is active, the owner can add/remove items and other
players can buy items.  When the shop is inactive, the owner can
only remove items, and no one can buy items.  A player's shop is
automatically set inactive when his/her bank account doesn't
cover monthly rent (can also be used for punishment).  Use this
command to re-open a shop that's been closed.
#105
DEATHTRAP
  A deathtrap is a room where you not only die, but your equipment is
unrecoverable.  Deathtraps are normal parts of the game and lost equipment will
not be reimbursed.  
 
  Deathtraps exist on Plague Island and in Undermountain.  Many exist somewhere
in the UnderDark.  Others may exist elsewhere, and new ones may exist in the
future.  If you're new to exploring and you're concerned about losing equipment,
temporarily give your equipment to a multi or trusted friend.  That way, if you
die, you lose only exp points and not your equipment.
 
  Remember: mud responsibly, look before you leap, and if you're not sure, don't
try it with all your equipment!
#0
FERN
   A fern increases your hitroll and damroll anywhere from +5 to +100 points.
It can only be obtained through immortal means, and its duration can be from
30 minutes to until you camp.  Depending on how a fern is set up (a spell, an
object, a trigger, etc.  ), its mechanics may vary.  For example, the fern
spell is saved when you camp but disappears if you die, whereas an immortal
setting hitroll/damroll disappears when you camp, but saves if you die.  
Ferns are usually announced ahead of time on board 5 or 6 or the motd.  Use
them responsibly and carefully since there are no reimbursements for losing a
fern.
