immreimb
How to reimb players:
 
First and MOST IMPORTANT is DO NOT GIVE PARTIAL REIMBS TO PLAYERS, e.g. DO NOT
REIMB ONE MULTI WITHOUT REIMBING THEM ALL.  I don't want to track individual
characters, I want to be able to say "Ziv was reimb'd" and it implies that his
four or eight or whatever multis were all reimb'd.
 
Second, a player should come to you AFTER their levels have been verified with
logs, and their name should be posted to board 5.  If it is not, DO NOT reimb
them!  They should have a good idea of what equipment and skills/spells they
want reimb'd.  If you don't think they know, you can tell them to get informed
and come back later.
 
If you are going to be online long enough to COMPLETELY reimb a player, read on.
 
- I don't care about the 2-multi limit for players getting a reimb, but they
  should camp down to 2 multis IMMEDIATELY AFTER a reimb.
 
- Use a "dressing room" for players (a no-exit room) to keep track of who is
  getting reimb'd to what.  One dressing room per real-life person might be good.
 
- Ask them each character's alignment and set it to what they ask.  DO NOT FORGET
  TO DO THIS STEP OR IT WILL SCREW UP THE EQ REIMB LATER.
 
- Purge their existing equipment.  They should be TOTALLY NAKED.
 
- Advance them to the level that will be posted on board 5.  If you have to reimb
  a remort, advance them to level 100, gremort them, force them to remort and
  repeat.  This ensures stat bonuses are put back correctly.
 
- Go to the room they are in and type "reimb <playername>".  This lets a player
  select the equipment and skills they want to be reimb'd.  Tell them to type
  "reimb" and to read the output and follow the instructions of "help reimb".
 
- Once a player is done selecting eq and skills/spells, they should type
  "reimb reimb!".  An [ INFO ] message is printed.  Gold is set at this point, too.
 
- Note: DO NOT set !hunger/!thirst for ANY PLAYER.  It's automatically set during
  gremorting to avatar.
 
- If a player is restored to level 102+, they should get a box labeled equipment
  (obj vnum 150).
 
- Once the reimb is complete, board post to board 9 that it's complete and I'll
  remove their "ticket" from board 5.
 
- If reimbursing an old player will conflict with an existing name (e.g. Sorian
  is both a 101 Ra and a 103 Ke), you can rename one of them AT THE TIME OF THE
  REIMB.  NOT BEFORE.
 
YOU ABSOLUTELY MUST MUST MUST MUST MAKE SURE THE EQUIPMENT A PLAYER REIMBS
ACTUALLY LOADS IN THE GAME.  THIS IS WHY IMMS ARE AN INTEGRAL PART OF THIS REIMB!
 
Objects from zones 0, 7, 8, 12, and 69 are automatically excluded, but some
builders put zone-testing objects in their zone.  For example, I could reimb
myself Cenwyc's earring of zone testing.  YOU MUST MAKE SURE THIS DOES NOT
HAPPEN.
 
We also reserve the right to refuse "absurd" equipment requests like the eye
of Jormungand.  *almost* anything else is acceptable (Lloth's nail is OK, gnoll
eq is OK, but note the fingerbone is now 2hr/1dr).
#115
reimburse
- You should know the name, level, race and class for each character you want
  reimb'd.
 
- You should board post that information to board 1.  See the other posts there
  for examples.
 
- You should know which skills and spells you want reimb'd for each character.
  Your character must be reimb'd to a level where he/she will learn that skill/
  spell.  For example, if you're reimbed a level 50 magic user, you can't be
  reimb'd the portal spell, which you'd learn at level 60.
 
- You should come up with a complete set of equipment that each character will be
  reimb'd.  Each character must be able to use the equipment in accordance with
  his/her race, class, alignment and level.  The code will guard against most
  of these, but if you reimb something you can't use, it will be junked with no
  replacement.
 
Details:
 
- Everyone gets one weapon, one shield and one holdable.  Regardless of dual-wield
  or if your character wants or uses a shield or holdable.
- You MUST know a SUBSTRING of each piece of equipment you want to reimb.
  Equipment databases such as Kelemvor's will be VERY useful for this.  You
  will enter these substrings and their slot, the game will put the appropriate
  object in the correct slot.
 
- If you can't remember the name of an object, immortals ARE NOT GOING TO HELP
  YOU.  Use players and databases BEFORE you ask for the reimb, NOT DURING.
- I will post another help file "help reimb2" with details on the reimb command.
 
The eq you reimb must actually in the game.  We reserve the right
to refuse specific equipment reimb requests on the basis of absurdity.  A
Lloth's nail is borderline acceptable.  The eye of Jormungand is not.  Gnoll eq
is acceptable, but note the fingerbone is now 2hr/1dr.
 
You must reimb all of your characters at the same time.  This is a one-time offer.
