#0
botting
   Anyone caught botting while AFK or AFW will be deleted.  Any gold,
equipment, (future) house ownership, (future) clan membership/leader, etc. will
be forfeit.  No appeals, no discussions, no arguments.
 
   Botting while AFK or AFW is defined as running triggers, scripts, or any
other form of automation while not actively paying attention to the output of
the triggers, scripts, etc.  Specifically, you should respond to questions from
players/imms in a reasonable amount of time.  I am leaving this as a somewhat
open-ended definition for the time being.
 
The following list is a subset of illegal things to bot while AFK/AFW:
 
    - Collecting gold
    - Practicing skills/spells
    - Killing mobs (exp bots)
    - Checking for objects loading
    - Brewing/scribing potions/scrolls
 
The following list is a subset of legal things to use while AFK/AFW:
 
    - Anti-idle triggers
    - Eat/drink triggers (this does not include create food/water triggers,
unless you already have the spell mastered or Ready to practice)
  
   There are two reasons for this policy.  First, botting while AFK/AFW
unbalances our world.  If botting while AFK/AFW were legal, I could write a
script to collect gold 24/7, I could make an unlimited supply of potions, I
could practice skills day and night, I could even script running zones for exp.
In contrast, if you are willing to sit and watch the bot run, you are
sacrificing your own time, and most likely won't spend more than a few hours a
day running it.
 
   Second, botting is incredibly difficult to catch.  We don't have an imm
staff to police people around the clock, and I can't code a bulletproof
algorithm to catch a bot for many different reasons.  Therefore, anyone caught
must be made an example of to strongly discourage others from botting while
AFK/AFW.
 
   If an imm claims that a player was botting while AFK/AFW, and the immortal
records a log of time-stamped text captured from the mud where the player was
asked to respond and didn't within a reasonable amount of time, the player in
question will be deleted.  This means imms need to be EXTREMELY careful who
they level an accusation of botting against.  There will be punishments for
purposefully misusing this power.

   ***addition added 10/27/2007 by Ceria
     -first time getting caught botting one week in freezer
     -second time is 1 week for you and your multis
     -third time is 2 weeks for you and your multis

   if you are dumb enough to get caught a forth time a punishment will be
   determined at that time.
