#125
TRIGEDIT

Usage:

> trigedit <virtual trigger number>
Edit/create triggers with virtual number specified.

> trigedit save <zone>
Save all triggers in zone to disk.

> trigedit save all
Save all trigger files which have been edited to disk.

Trigedit is the trigger editor portion of OLC.  Trigedit allows you
to edit all aspects of triggers (scripts) in the game.  You will
only be allowed to edit/create triggers in the zone for which you
have permissions.  You will only be allowed to attach the triggers
once you have the DGATTACH flag.

See Also: OASIS OLC GEDIT OEDIT REDIT SEDIT ZEDIT EDITOR
#104
SING

Syntax: sing [level] '<spell name>' [target]

The bard casting a spell will need to sing it, with the sing command.
The optional [level] refers to the level of the spell being sang.

For example:

> sing 1'inspire' koan
> sing 10'fire song' turaylon
> sing 'sanctuary' grundox

If [level] is omitted, the sing command will cast the spell at the current
skill level of the caster.  If the spell is cast at a higher level than the
current skill level, the cast may face dire consequences.

If [target] is omitted then the spell is cast upon the caster.

The special keywords "tank" and "target" can be used for [target].  

For example:

> sing 'dragon' tank
This will cast the spell 'dragon' on the tank in a fight.

> sing 'enfeeble' target
This will cast the enfeeble spell on whoever the tank is fighting.

See Also: PRACTICE LEARN CAST
