BUILDING

This help file lists various help files which are of use to
builders on Phoenix.  To view more detailed help on any of these
commands, type HELP <KEYWORD>.

OASIS--This is the introductory help file for Oasis OLC.  Every
	builder should read this file.

OLC--Help for the 'olc' command which shows which parts of the world
	have been unsaved.

MEDIT
REDIT
GEDIT
OEDIT--These are the individual modules of Oasis OLC.
SEDIT
ZEDIT

MOBPROGS--Help file for the mobprogs scripting language.

IMMUNITIES
SUSCEPTIBILITIES--Describes how Immunities, Resistances, and 
RESISTANCES       Susceptibilities work.

WEAP_PROF--Describes how weapon types relate to weapon proficiency skills.

EDITOR--Describes the text editor used for building, boards, mail, etc.
	The editor has many useful search and replace commands for the
	builder.

FORMS
PROGRESS FORM--These forms need to be filled out and returned to your
COMPLETED FORM    building manager on a regular basis.

SPECS--Help file describing the function of each spec proc available for
	mobiles.

OLIST
MLIST--Describes the listing commands for Objects, Mobs, and Rooms.
RLIST

VWEAR--Describes the 'vwear' command which lists equipment by body positions.

SHOW--Describes the 'show' command.  Many of the show options are very useful
	to builders.

STANDARDS--Lists various standards expected from PhoenixMUD builders.  This is
	an extremely important informational command to read.

PURGE--Describes the 'purge' command.  Used to clear a room of its contents.

IDLE--Describes the 'idle' command, used to idle out a zone from memory.

ZRESET--Describes the 'zreset' command, used to reset a zone.

ATTACH/DETACH--Describes how to attach or detach scripts to rooms, mobs,
	or objects.
