#104
IMMUNITIES IMMUNE RESIST RESISTANCES SUSC SUSCEPTIBILITIES
 
The immunity/resistance/susceptible bitvector effect how much damage an
attack will do.  Immunity to a certain type of attack means that you will
take 1/16 of the intended damage.  Resistance means you take 1/2 damage.
Susceptibility means you take 2x the damage the attack normally inflicts.
The bitvectors affect saving throws, if applicable, by the same amount.
 
Here are the bitvectors and some examples of the type of attack they
represent.
 
FIRE   - All heat/fire based attacks.  
	Ex. fireball, flame strike, burning hands, dragon's breath, 
	flaming/desert sectors.
COLD   - All cold/freeze based attacks. 
	Ex. chill touch, frost blast
ELEC   - All electrical/lightning based attacks. 
	Ex. lightning bolt, shocking grasp.
ENERGY - Any magic attack that causes direct harm to the victim. 
	Ex. earthquake, color spray.
ACID   - Any acid/decay based attack. 
	Ex. acid blast, acid room sectors.
DRAIN  - Any attack that drains the will to live from its victim.
	Ex. enfeeble, energy drain, dispel good/evil, undead's touch.
POISON - Any attack that inflicts damage with poison.
	Ex. poison, gas blast
HOLY   - Any good-aligned spell.
	Ex. wrath of god, dispel evil
UNHOLY - Any evil-aligned spell.
	Ex. harm, dispel good
SLEEP  - Any attack that will cause the victim to lose consciousness
CHARM  - Any attack that will cause the victim to lose control of their own
         actions.
HOLD   - Any attack that leaves the victim awake but unable to move.
BLUNT  - Any damage by a blunt object. Includes the weapon types: HIT,
         BLUDGEON, BLAST, CRUSH, POUND, MAUL, PUNCH, kick, headbutt
PIERCE - Any sharp attack made by a thrusting motion. Includes the weapon
         types: PIERCE, PIERCE_NO_BS, BITE, STING, STAB
SLASH  - Any sharp attack made by a swinging motion. Includes the weapon
         types: SLASH, WHIP, CLAW, THRASH
 
For all the above attack types, if you set the same bit in more than one
bitvector, the effects will be combined. 
immunity & resistance(don't combine): 1/16
immunity & susceptibility: 1/8 
resistance & susceptibility: 1/1  
immunity & resistance & susceptibility: 1/8
 
The following 5 vectors are influenced by the magic level of the weapon
causing the damage, and/or the level of the NPC.  Which of these flags will
affect your attack is decided by the following formula:
If you are a PC and hitting with TYPE_HIT (bare handed) 
   you hit with no magic bonus
Your magic bonus = your highest hitroll or damroll of both the weapons you
   are wielding. i.e. if you are wielding a +1+2 sword your magic bonus is
   +2. if you are also wielding a +4+1 dagger, your bonus is +4.
If you are a mob your bonus is your level/20(rounded down) or your bonus 
   from magical weapons, whichever is higher

NONMAG - effect people with a bonus of 0 (mobs level  1-19)
PLUS1  - effect people with a bonus of 1 (mobs level 20-39)
PLUS2  - effect people with a bonus of 2 (mobs level 40-59)
PLUS3  - effect people with a bonus of 3 (mobs level 60-79)
PLUS4  - effect people with a bonus of 4 (mobs level 80-99)
 
* These do not stack. if(immune) dam/16 else if(resist) dam/2 else
   if(susc) dam*2.  There is no immunity or resistance against attackers with
   a bonus of greater than 4.  But, if the attack has a bonus>4 and you are
   susceptible to PLUS4, then you take the extra damage for these attacks as
   well.
 
As a general rule, here is how items/spells that affect these flags should
be level based:
       NONMAG  PLUS1  PLUS2  PLUS3  PLUS4
IMMUN  30      50     70     90     never
RESIST 15-20   35-40  55-60  75-80  95
 
* If you have an item add immunity to one weapon type have it make the user
  susceptible to a couple of others for balance.
