#0
AUCTION BID NOAUCTION

Usage: auction <item> <asking price>
       bid <no arg|your bid>

AUCTION and BID allow people to utilize the auctioning system in the game.
In order to auction an item using the AUCTION command, the item must be
in your inventory.  The aucioner must remain in the game during the length
of the auction.  The mud will not allow you to auction an item which had been
previously donated, as this is considered extremely rude.  All auctioning
is anonymous--that is no one knows who is auctioning and bidding.

The mud will prevent overpriced auctions by limiting the asking price to ten
times the item's value plus ten coins.  Thus, if an item is valued at 1000
coins, the maximum initial asking price will be 100,10 coins.

To bid on the item being auctioned, use the BID command.  Typing bid without
an argument will allow a free identify of the item being sold.  Auctioners
cannot, of course, bid on their own items.  All bids will be drawn first from
the gold the player has on hand and then from the player's bank account. 
Also, in order to prevent drawn out auctions where people outbid each other by
small amounts of coins, the mud will require a bid of 5% or 5000 coins more than
the previous bid, whichever is less.

Auctions are done on a 'going once, going twice, going three times, sold' system.
The bid command without an argument will also display the current status of the
auction.   There is currently no way for a player to stop an auction they
have started, nor a way to withdraw a bid.  If the auctioner leaves the game
before the auction is over, the item will be forfeit.

The NOAUCTION command will prevent you from seeing what is happening on the 
auction channel.

See Also: VALUE
#0
CAMP CAMP!

Usage: camp (while in an outdoors type room)
Usage: camp! (while in an outdoors type room)

Camping is used to leave the game at PhoenixMUD.  Just go to an outside room
and issue the CAMP command.  You cannot camp with certain items in your inventory,
you will be notified if you have one of these items.  There is a limit to the 
number of items you can camp with, you can camp with no more than 200 items.
To do so puts you in jeopardy of losing all or some of the items.

If you just wish to camp out and not be notified that you have non-campable items
in your inventory, use the CAMP! command.  This will drop any such items to the
floor and camp you out.

At some point in the future camp will be modified so there is a slight chance
of losing some items.  When this happens you will have the option of renting
instead which will prevent any loss but cost a nominal fee.

See Also: RENT COUNT INN
#0
GOSSIP . GRATS OOC NOGOSSIP NOGRATS NOOOC

Usage: gossip <message>
       grats <message>
       ooc <message>

These are channels reserved for specific purposes.  Messages on these
channels reach everyone who is monitoring them.  

Examples:

  > gossip Art thou willing to adventure with thee?
  > grats LEVEL!!!!!!!!
  > grats GRATS CATJE!!!!!!!!
  > ooc Hey, did anyone catch that piece on CNN??

See also: EMOTE, GSAY, HOLLER, NOREPEAT, SAY, SHOUT
#0
AUTOASSIST

Usage: autoassist

This command toggles whether or not you automatically assist other group members
when they enter combat.  You must be a member of the group in order for this to
work.  The same restrictions to regular combat and assisting (standing, non-
peaceful room, etc) apply.

See also: TOGGLE AUTOSPLIT AUTOGOLD AUTOLOOT AUTOEXIT AUTOSACRIFICE ASSIST
#0
AUTOGOLD AUTOLOOT AUTOSPLIT

Usage: autogold

This commands toggles automatic gold looting.  When autogold is on, if you strike the
killing blow on a mob you will automatically loot the mob's corpse for its gold.
Tip: Use autogold rather than autoloot in an area where the mobs have gold, but no
equipment which you want.

Usage: autoloot

This command toggles automatic gold looting.  When autoloot is on and you strike the
killing blow on a mob, you will automatically loot the mob's corpse for all of its
possessions, including gold.  Autoloot takes precedence over autogold.  That is,
autoloot must be turned off if you wish to only use autogold.

Usage: autosplit

The autosplit command splits all money you loot from a corpse to the members of your
group.  This command is executed immediately after looting gold from a corpse.

See Also: AUTOEXIT AUTOSACRIFICE AUTOASSIST TOGGLE
#0
AUTOEXIT

Usage: autoexit

Toggles the automatic display of currently available exits.  Not all
possible exits will be displayed, only those immediately available.
If a door is closed it will not show up as a possible exit.

See also: TOGGLE AUTOGOLD AUTOLOOT AUTOSPLIT AUTOSACRIFICE AUTOASSIST
#0
AUTOSACRIFICE

Usage: autosacrifice

This command toggles automatic sacrificing of corpses after they are killed.
Autogold and autoloot will happen before autosacrifice, but bewere that if
you cannot carry the weight of the items from the looting, they will be lost after
the corpse is sacrificed.

See also: TOGGLE AUTOEXIT AUTOASSIST AUTOGOLD AUTOLOOT AUTOSPLIT SACRIFICE
#0
BANK WITHDRAW DEPOSIT BALANCE

Commands to take money out of the bank, put money in the bank, or see how
much money you have in the bank.

Examples:

  > deposit 400
  > withdraw 1000
  > balance

See also: GOLD, SCORE
#0
BOARD BOARDS

This command allows access to the "virtual" bulletin boards available
on the mud.  We have done away with physical boards and the need to
move from room to room to read varous boards.  The BOARD command will
allow you access to all appropriate boards anywhere in the game.  You
will have access only to certain boards of course.  (i.e. Only clan 
members will have access to clan bulletin boards.)
 
BOARD COMMANDS:
 
board           -       Will list the commands available for the board.

board list      -       Will show you a list of all available boards.
 
board switch    -       Will allow you to switch between the multiple
                        boards on the mud. (See 'board list')
                          Usage: board switch <board number>
                          Ex   : board switch 4
 
board write     -       Will post a message to the current board.
                          Usage: board write <header>
                          Ex:    board write Attention all players
 
board look      -       Will show you a list of all messages posted
                        on the selected board.
 
board read      -       Will allow you to read a specific message on
                        the selected board.
                          Usage: board read <message number>
                          Ex:    board read 4

board remove    -       Will allow you to remove a message that you
                        have posted, for immortals and above will
                        allow you to remove a message from any board
                        you have access to.
                          Usage: board remove <message number>
                          Ex:    board remove 4

See Also: EDITOR
#0
BRIEF

Usage: brief

Toggle "brief mode".  When in brief mode, you don't see the descriptions of
the room you are in; only the name of the room and the people and objects
there.  Unless you're very familiar with the area in which you're traveling,
however, it is not advisable to use this command.  Frequently, you will find
small but vital hints in the descriptions of the rooms: An extra peek at your
surroundings could mean the difference between life and death!

If you explicitly type 'look', you will always see the full room description,
even in BRIEF mode.

See also: COMPACT, LOOK
#0
BUG TYPO IDEA
BUG TYPO IDEA
 
Usage: bug <bug report>
       idea <your new idea>
       typo <that nasty typo>       
 
For making useful suggestions and reporting problems to the Powers that Be.
 
Examples:
  > bug the entire game crashes when I type 'put bag in bag'
  > idea make a restaurant in Aethelfyrd
  > typo 'sence' should be spelled 'sense'
 
When making an idea, please keep the following in mind:
 
- Be as specific as possible.  It's your idea, please convey it as
  clearly, concisely and supply as much detail as you can.  Include
  examples when possible.
 
- Keep the balance of the whole game in mind.  We're not going to
  implement a cool idea if it unbalances classes or races.
 
- We're not going to make PhoenixMud "not PhoenixMud".  We have too
  many existing characters to modify the existing class and race system, 
  practice system, etc.
 
- Be practical.  We're looking for ideas that have a lot of "bang for
  your buck".  An idea that takes a hundred hours of coding but results
  in only a minor changes for players may not be worth it.
#0
BUY

Usage: buy <item name>
       buy #<item number>
       buy n.<item name>
       buy n <item name>
       buy n #<item number>

If you'd like to purchase an item from a shop and have the money, you can buy
it.  Items can be bought by name, or by their number in the shop listing,
and can be bought in quantity.
 
Examples:
 
  > buy sword        (buy the first sword on the list)
  > buy #3           (buy the third item on the list)
  > buy 4.sword      (buy the fourth sword on the list)
  > buy 10 bread     (buy 10 pieces of bread)
  > buy 10 #2        (buy 10 of the second item on the list)
 
See also: LIST, SELL, SHOPS, VALUE
#0
CAST

Syntax: cast [level] '<spell name>' [target]

Spell caster use the cast command to cast spells.  The optional [level] 
refers to the level of the spell being brewed.  

For example:

> cast 1 'heal' frodo
> cast 10 'heal' frodo
> cast 'heal' frodo

If [level] is omitted, the cast command will cast the spell at the current 
skill level of the caster.  If the spell is cast at a higher level then the
current skill level, the cast may face dire consequences.

If [target] is omitted then the spell is cast upon the caster.

The special keywords "tank" and "target" can be used for [target].  

For example:

> cast 'heal' tank
This will cast a heal spell on the tank in a fight.

> cast 'harm' target
This will cast a harm spell on whoever the tank is fighting.

See Also: PRACTICE LEARN SING
#0
CLEAR CLS

Clears the screen.
#0
COMMANDS

Usage: commands

The COMMANDS command gives a canonical list of all the known verbs.

Each command listed should have help available by typing "HELP <command>".

See also: SOCIAL, SOCIALS
#0
COMPACT

Usage: compact

This command toggles the extra blank line output to your screen after each
command.  Useful if you have a small display.

See also: BRIEF
#0
COMMUNE

Usage: commune <message>

Commune will allow a mortal to send a message to all gods currently logged in.
Only the logged in gods at the time will see your message, so it is a private 
channel to communicate with the god staff, especially when they are invisible.  
When a god communes, all mortals in the game will see the message.  Commune 
cannot be turned off like other communication channels.
#0
CONSIDER

Usage: consider <monster>

This command will compare your Level with the <monster>'s level.  You will then
receive a rough estimate, which is by no means exact.  Consider does not take
hitpoints/special attacks/damage into account.

Example:

  > consider fido

See also: HIT, KILL, DIAGNOSE
#0
COUNT

Usage: count [character]

The COUNT command counts the total number of objects you have in your possession.
This will aid in you in making sure you do not go over the renting limits.  For
gods, count followed by a character's name will tell you how many objects that
person is carrying.

See Also: RENT, CAMP
#0
DIAGNOSE

Usage: diagnose [character]

The DIAGNOSE command tells you how wounded a character looks.  If you are
fighting someone, you can use DIAGNOSE with no arguments to diagnose the
person you're fighting.

Examples: 

  > diagnose
  > diagnose rasmussen

See also: CONSIDER
#0
DISPLAY PROMPT

Usage: prompt < H | M | V | A | G | X | T | all | none >

The display or prompt commands allow you to customize what you see on your 
on-screen prompt.   The prompt will automatically add your condition and
the mob's condition while you are in combat.  It will return to normal after
combat ends.  You will still see the prompt options you choose.  Note that
the prompt and the infobar are mutually exclusive.  The perform the same 
function except in a different way.  

The Prompt options are:
	H		Display hit points
	M		Display mana (energy) points
	V		Display movement points
	A		Display current alignment
	G		Display gold on hand
	X		Display experience points
	T		Display maximum values for H,M,V
	all		Display all of the above items
	none		Display only the > character

See also: TOGGLE INFOBAR
#0
DONATE

Usage: donate <object>
       donate <number> coins


This command takes an object that you no longer want and deposits it in a
random donation room throughout the realms to assist newbies in getting
started.  There is a 75% chance objects donated will wind up in a
donation room, and a 25% chance the item will be junked.

  > donate shield
  > donate all.bread
  > donate 500 coins

See also: JUNK CDONATE
#0
DROP

Usage: drop <item>
       drop all.<item>
       drop all
       drop <number> coins

If you lose interest in a carried item, you can drop it on the ground.

  > drop bottle
  > drop all.bread
  > drop all
  > drop 1000 coins

See also: DONATE, GET, JUNK
