NOSHOUT

Usage: noshout

NOSHOUT toggles whether or not you hear shouts.  (deaf) will appear after
your name in the WHO list.

See also: FLAGS, HOLLER, SHOUT, TOGGLE, WHO
#0
NOSUMMON

Usage: nosummon

Due to problems we've had with players killing other players by summoning
them to Bad Places, all characters now have SUMMON PROTECTION turned on by
default.  This prevents people from summoning you and gives you a warning
message if someone tries.  If you want to let someone summon you (i.e. if
someone wants to summon you for a legitimate reason), type NOSUMMON to turn
off summon protection.  You can then type NOSUMMON again to turn protection
back on.

See also: SUMMON, TOGGLE
#0
NOTELL

Usage: notell

Use NOTELL if you wish to prevent other players from using "tell" to
communicate with you.  (notell) will appear after your name in the WHO
list if you have notell on.

See also: FLAGS, TELL, TOGGLE, WHO
#0
OFFER RENT

Usage: offer
       rent

For use in the receptions of inns.

This command is currently not implemented.

See also: INN, COUNT, CAMP
#0
OPEN CLOSE LOCK UNLOCK

Usage: open | close | lock | unlock <door> [direction]

To open, close, lock, and unlock doors, of course.

Examples:

  > open portal
  > lock door
  > unlock door south
  > close gate

See also: ENTER, LEAVE
#0
ORDER

Usage: order <character> <command>
       order followers <command>

Used for ordering pets and charmed people to do your evil bidding.  You
can order everyone under your command with "order followers".

Examples:

  > order puppy eat bread
  > order cityguard sleep

See also: CHARM
#0
POUR

Usage: pour <from container> <to container>
       pour <from container> out

If you want to pour some liquid from one container to another.  Pouring
out simply empties the contents of the container onto the ground.

Examples:

  > pour canteen cup
  > pour cup out

See also: FILL
#0
PRACTICE LEARN

The system of learning skills and spells has completely changed in Phoenix 4.0.
There are no longer practice 'slots' that you accumulate as you level and spend
on learning skills and spells.  Now, you learn by using your spells and skills.
As you gain levels, new skills and spells will become available to you.  Go to
your guildmaster and type LEARN <skill/spell name> to gain that skill/spell for the
first time.  The PRACTICE command can be used outside of a guild room to determine
what spells/skills you can learn and at what level you currently know them.

After learning a skill/spell initially, go out and use it.  You will gain a small
percentage of ability by using the skills and spells.   Of course, you will learn
more by your failures than by your successes.  Intelligence, Wisdom, and Dexterity
are very important to improving your skills and spells.

After learning on your own for a while, you will receive a message telling you to
go to your guildmaster to further practice.  At your guildmaster, you can use the
PRACTICE command to improve your spell or skill further.  You will have the ability
to practice the skill at the guildmaster once per level you have gained above the
level when you first learned the spell or skill.   Example:  You learn BASH at level
8.  You may use the practice command once for level 9, once for level 10 and so on.
This is assuming you have learned enough about the spell or skill on your own.

Finally, guildmasters now charge for learning and practicing spells and skills. Make
sure you bring a lot of money with you.

See also: EXPERIENCE GAIN CAST
#0
PULL

Usage: pull <grenade item>

Pull is used to activate a grenade type item before throwing it.  Each grenade
has a specific countdown timer.  You must throw the grenade before the timer goes
off or it will explode in your hands.  You must wield the grenade before pulling
the pin.

See Also: THROW SHOOT RANGED
#0
PUT

Usage: put <item> <container>
       put all.<item> <container>
       put all <container>

For putting items into containers.

Examples:

  > put bread bag
  > put all.bread bag
  > put all chest

Note: You can now put/get items from equipment which you are wearing
without having to remove the item first.

See also: GET
#0
QSAY

Usage: qsay <message>

To tell something to everyone on the current Quest.

See also: QUEST
#0
QUAFF POTION POTIONS

Usage: quaff <potion>

Quaff is used to "drink" a (magical) potion.  The magic will take effect
immediately, for better or for worse...

See also: SWALLOW
#0
QUEST

Usage: quest

This simple toggle command merely informs the Powers that Be that you
wish to participate in the currently running Quest.  If an immortal
is running a Quest and needs to know who wishes to participate, he/she
will ask players to turn on their Quest flags using this QUEST command
if they are interested in the Quest.  It also allows you to listen in on
the quest channel and receive information specific to the quest.

See also: QSAY
#0
QUIT QUIT!

When you get tired of playing, you can leave the game by typing 'quit!'
(with the !). Note that quitting this way will cause any items you might 
be carrying to simply be left on the ground.  You are better off to 
save and camp.

See also:  See also: INN, OFFER, RENT, CAMP 
#0
RACESKILLS

Usage: raceskills

This command simply lists the various innate skills which races have
and at what levels they gain them.

See Also: REMORTS RACES
#0
READ

Usage: read <object>

When you want to read something.

Example:

  > read note

See also: BOARDS
#0
RECALL

Usage: recall

The RECALL command brings you back to your hometown safely.  Recall takes
half of your movement and mana points as a 'sacrifice' to the gods for 
the transportation.  Note that recall is provided as a service for low
level characters only.   After level 16, you will not be able to use
the recall command for 'free'.   At that point you must begin to carry
scrolls of recall or learn spells such as word of recall.  The MUD will
display a warning to this effect every time you use recall below level 16.
#0
RECITE SCROLL SCROLLS

Usage: recite <scroll> [Target]

Is used to "read" a magical scroll.  Target can be an object, character or
nothing (which may be yourself).

See also: SPELLS
#0
REFUEL

Usage: refuel <light> <fuel>

Refuel is used to refuel certain light sources.  There are currently three
types of fuel in the game, oil, fat, and coal.  Lights will only take one
of these fuel types, if they can be refueled at all.

See Also: LIGHT FUEL
#0
REMORT! REMORT_COMMAND

OVERVIEW
  The remort! command allows a player who is level 101 (Hero), 102 (Angel), or
103 (Avatar) to continue leveling (see "help remort_test" for how to become a
Hero, Angel or Avatar).  Using this command sets your character back to level 1,
but with a race or class not previously available.  Remorts get bonuses such as
better equipment, more hitpoints and mana, or learning skills earlier.  However,
the amount of experience points needed to level increases each time you remort.
.
Note: You must remove all equipment prior to remorting.

REMORT for HEROES
  At level 101, you have two options: remort to the same class (SCR), or remort
to a new class unavailable to non-remorts (DCR).  Make this decision with care
since it affects the races and classes available to your character the next
time he or she remorts.  As a general guideline, if you are interested in
roleplaying and/or uniqueness, consider SCR.  If you are interested in
powerplaying, consider DCR (also called traditional remorting).
.
REMORT PATHS
  1: Non-remort -> same-class remort (SCR) -> same-race remort (SRR)
  2: Non-remort -> class remort (DCR) -> race remort (DRR) -> triple remort (TR)
.
REMEMBERING FAMILIAR SKILLS/SPELLS
  When you remort, you forget all your skills/spells.  However, if you SCR,
SRR, DRR or TR, when you learn the skill again, it will be at the proficiency
your character had during his or her previous remort.
.
  For example, A Hero human monk has mastered stun.  When he or she SCRs, he
loses the ability to stun until level 43.  At level 43, he will learn the stun
skill as mastered.
.
  Another example, an angel necromancer has waterwalk at level 7.  When she DRRs,
she loses the ability to cast waterwalk until level 5 when she will learn the
waterwalk spell at spell level 7.
.
SAME CLASS REMORT (SCR) - Use the "remort! same" command
  * Class name change
      Warrior -> Elite Warrior, Cleric -> Priest, Thief -> Rogue,
      Magic User -> Wizard, Range -> Warder, Bard -> Troubadour,
      Monk -> Sensei, Barbarian -> Berserker, Paladin -> Templar,
      Anti-Paladin -> Dark Templar, Druid -> Archdruid
  * +1 to hitpoints, mana and move each level
  * +2 stat points, determined by class
      Wa: +1 to str/con, Cl: +1 to int/wis, Th: +1 to int/dex,
      Mu: +1 to int/wis, Ra: +1 to wis/con, Bd: +1 to int / +3 to cha
      Mo: +1 to int/con, Ba: +1 to str/con, Pa: +1 to str/wis,
      AP: +1 to str/int, Dr: +1 to int/wis
  * Note: stat increases will not increase above your racial maximum (e.g. a
      human thief with 18 dex will not have 19 dex after SCR).  See "help races"
      for the racial maximums and abilities of each race.
  * No alignment restriction to cast spells (e.g. neutral paladin)
  * Learn skills/spells 15% earlier than non-remorts
  * Exp per level is same as traditional first remorts (DCRs).  Slightly less
      than twice the non-remort exp per level.

.
DIFFERENT CLASS REMORT (DCR) - Use the "remort! <class>" command
  * Available DCR classes: Necromancer, Deva, Kensai and Assassin
  * Increased hitpoints, mana and move each level (depends on the class)
  * +2 stat points, determined by class
      Ne: +1 to int/wis, De: +1 to int/wis, Ke: +1 to str/con, As: +1 to dex/int
  * Note: stat increases will not increase above your racial maximum (e.g. a
      human thief with 18 dex will not have 19 dex after SCR).  See "help races"
      for the racial maximums and abilities of each race.
  * Good-aligned necromancers and evil-aligned devas can't cast spells.
  * See "skills <class>" and "spells <class>" to see what skills and spells
      these classes learn and when.
  * Exp per level is slightly less than twice the non-remort exp per level.
.
DOUBLE REMORT - Use the "remort! <race>" command.
  * Available DCR races: Draconian, Aesir, Titan and Shadow
  * Increased hitpoints, mana and move each level (depends on the race)
  * All DCR races have racial maximums of 20 for all stats.
  * +1 to str/int/wis/dex/con, plus one extra stat by race:
      Drc: +1 int, Shd: +1 dex, Ttn: +1 str, Asr: +1 wis
  * Note: stat increases will not increase above your racial maximum.
  * See "help races" to see each races' skills/spells/abilities.
  * All DCR races get infravision.
  * Exp per level is double the first remort exp per level.
  * Can wear equipment with level restrictions "Remort X" once you are level
    X or higher, unless the equipment is flagged anti- your race or class.
    One example, all evil SCRs can wear the "iron cross".
  * Upon reaching level 103, you do not need to eat or drink, but you can
      still get drunk.
.
SAME RACE REMORT (SRR) - Use the "remort! same" command.
  * You keep all the bonuses of SCR, plus...
  * Final mortal level is 103 (Avatar), no third remorting allowed.
  * +1 to hitpoints, mana and move each level
  * +1 to all stats (str/int/wis/con/dex/cha)
  * Racial max becomes 20, stat increases will not go above racial max.
  * Infravision
  * Exp per level is same as traditional second remorts (DRRs).
  * Can wear equipment with level restrictions "Double Remort X" once
      you are level X or higher, unless the equipment is flagged anti- your
      race or class.  One example, all SRRs can use Raiden's Death Cloak.
  * Upon reaching level 103, you do not need to eat or drink, but you can
      still get drunk.
  * There will be no guarantee of adding equipment, resists, skills or
      abilities.
.
TRIPLE REMORT - Use the "remort! same" command.
  * +1 to hitpoints, mana and move each level
  * +1 to all stats with a racial maximum of 20
  * Use equipment regardless of alignment, race or class restriction flags.
  * No alignment restriction for casting spells (e.g. evil deva)
  * Exp requirement is 4x double remort.
  * See "help unremort" in case you change your mind.
  * Final mortal level is 104 (Demi-god).
  * The remort test for triple remort has not been designed yet.
