#104
AMBUSH

syntax: ambush <mob>

Ambush will allow a player who is wielding a weapon to sneak up on a 
mob and attack it from the rear surprising it. 
#0
AXE

The Axe skill helps a character hit mobs with axe type weapons.
#0
BACKSTAB

Backstab is a way to sneak up on a person and attempt to place your dagger 
in his back, at exactly the point where it does most damage.  A successful 
backstab gives a damage multiplier, depending on level:

The chance of successfully backstabbing a person depends on how well you have 
practiced backstab at your guild.  You can always backstab sleeping people.
#0
BANDAGE

Syntax: bandage <person>

When a player is bandaged they will regenerate hitpoints and mana at an 
increased rate.
#0
BASH

Syntax: bash <mob>

The success of a bash depends upon how well you are learned. To bash someone 
is to attempt to 'knock' that person over. If you succeed you will inflict 
minor damage, and cause the victim to fall on it's rear. The victim will be 
unable to issue any commands for 2 rounds of violence. If you miss you 
loose your balance and fall. A bash makes you unable to type commands for 
2 rounds of violence. Note that hitting a person who is resting/sitting 
will inflict more damage.
#0
BERSERK

Syntax: berserk

It will causes you to hit every mob in the room at the same time. It can  
be very powerful and very dangerous. Use it carefully.
#0
BLOCK

After you learn block you will become proficient in the skill and it will 
become automatic during a fight. Block is based on chance, dexterity, 
level, and practiced level.
#0
BOW

The Bow skill helps a character hit mobs with bow type weapons.
#0
BREW

Syntax: brew <container> [level] <spell>

Brew allows a character to make potions. Not all spells can be made 
into a potion.

[level] is optional and refers to the level of the spell being brewed.  

For example:

> brew bottle 1 heal
> brew bottle 5 heal
> brew bottle heal

If [level] is omitted, the brew command will brew a potion at the current 
skill level of the caster.
#0
CAMOUFLAGE

The Camouflage is similar to the Hide skill, but works much better in 
the wilderness (10%-20% better) and much worse in a city (50% worse).  

See also: Hide
#0
CHANT

Syntax: chant

When you begin chanting your hitpoints and mana will increase at a 
higher rate. You must remain in the chanting position for this to continue 
to work. If you stand, sit, sleep, etc you will break the chant.
#0
CIRCLE

Circle allows you to backstab a mob while you are fighting, as long as  
you are not the person taking the damage from the mob. You must have 
learned the back stab skill for this skill to be effective. Effectively 
this skill may only be used when you are in a group. You get the same 
damage bonus as backstab when you are successful. 
