CLUB

The Club skill helps a character hit mobs with club type weapons.
#0
CROSSBOW

The Crossbow skill helps a character hit mobs with crossbow type weapons.
#0
DAGGER

The Dagger skill helps a character hit mobs with dagger type weapons.
#0
DARKEN

Syntax: darken

This will reduce a characters light level, hence reducing the overall 
light in the room.

See Also: LIGHTEN
#0
DISARM

Syntax: disarm <mob name>

When used this skill will allow you to disarm a mob of its weapon. You 
must be wielding a weapon to make it a success. Success is based on 
dexterity, Level, and skill level. Once disarmed the weapon will go into 
the mobs inventory.
#0
DISMOUNT

Syntax: dismount

This command allows you to dismount from the mob that you are riding.

See Also: MOUNT RIDING TAME
#0
DODGE

This skill helps the character dodge attacks.  Higher skill level, 
character level, and dexterity will improve this skill.
#0
"DUAL WIELD"

Allows the character to wield more than one weapon.  The heaviest weapon 
is automatically used as the primary weapon.  The secondary weapon is 
used periodically during a fight.
#0
FISTICUFFS

The Fisticuffs skill helps a character hit mobs with bare hands.
#0
FOURTH ATTACK

Lets the character hit up to four times per fight round.  Actual number 
of hit per round is determined by skill level and a random factor.
#0
GORE

Gore is similar to headbutt, but for characters with horns (like minotaurs).

See Also: HEADBUTT
#0
HAMMER

The Hammer skill helps a character hit mobs with hammer type weapons.
#0
HEADBUTT

Syntax: headbutt <mob name>

This skill will allow you to do damage to a mob during a fight by 
headbutting them.
#0
HIDE

When you type hide there is a chance that you hide in the room. If 
hidden you can only be "sensed" by the "sense life" spell. Even if sensed 
your identity will remain hidden. Hide is broken by pressing return, regardless 
of whether you typed a command or not.

Example:

 > hide
 Ok.
 > (you wait for ex. 5 mins and remain hidden for 5 mins)

 > (You pressed enter and no longer hide)
#0
KICK

The success of a kick depends upon how well you are learned. The higher 
level you reach the harder you kick. There is one small catch -- whenever 
you kick (or miss) you will be unable to type any command for three rounds 
of 'Violence' -- so be sure that you do not need to flee!
#0
LAY_HANDS

Syntax: lay_hands <player name>

This skill will transfer hit points from a yourself to a wounded victim. 
You will in turn receive the wounds of the victim.
#0
LIGHTEN

Syntax: lighten

This skill increases the level of a characters light, hence it increases 
the amount of light in the room over all.

See also: DARKEN
#0
MEDITATE

Meditation helps the character to regenerate faster.
#0
MOUNT

Syntax: mount <mob>

This skills allows the character to mount a horse or other mountable mob.
Some mobs may have to be tamed with the TAME skill before they will allow
players to ride them.

See also: RIDING DISMOUNT TAME
#0
PALM

Syntax: palm <object name>

This skill will allow a player to take an object off the ground without 
showing any messages to the room. There is a chance that this could fail 
as in any skill and messages would be displayed to the room.
#0
PARRY

This skill lets the character use his/her weapon to block, or parry, 
an attack.  Higher skill level, character level, and dexterity will help 
a character successfully parry an attack.
