#0
SOCIALS

Usage: <social> [<victim>]

Socials are commands used to show your affective state to others.  The
actor, victim and bystanders may receive different messages.  Generally,
social commands are used only to express emotion and not to take action,
but it is possible that some mobs (or players) will take action based on
the social.  (Slap a dragon lately?)

Example:

  > shake homer
  > applaud marge
  > stare

The SOCIALS command generates a canonical listing of all available socials.

  > socials

See also: EMOTE
#0
"ACID BLAST"

Syntax: cast 'Acid Blast' <target>

When cast, a stream of corrosive acid streams from the caster's fingers to
hit one target.  The corrosive properties of the acid will cause great harm
to the target, as the acid burns most anything, although a few mobs out
there may show some resistance.  As the caster gains experience casting
Acid Blast, the acid become more potent, doing more harm.
#0
"ANIMATE DEAD"

Syntax: cast 'Animate Dead' <target>

Animate dead causes the dead to animate and follow the spell caster.
#0
ARMOR

Syntax: cast 'Armor' <target>

Creates a magical shield about one person which helps repel physical attacks.
#0
ATONEMENT

Syntax: cast 'Atonement' <target>

The target of an Atonement is forgiven sins and granted alignment as determined by the caster's alignment.  The atonement is not without cost for the target, as s/he must sacrifice some experience to prove his/her worth.
#0
"BARK SKIN"

Syntax: cast 'Bark Skin' <target>

Turns your skin to bark, making you harder to hit.
#0
BLESS

Syntax: cast 'Bless' <target>

When cast on a target, the target is more righteous, thus allowing the target to hit better.  The target also receives a modest amount of protection from spells.
#0
BLINDNESS

Syntax: cast 'Blindness' <target>

Blindness will blind a victim, making them, well, blind.
#0
BLUR

Syntax: cast 'Blur' <target>

Blur makes the target move faster, thus the target is able to hit victims faster.
#0
"BURNING HANDS"

Syntax: cast 'Burning Hands' <target>

Causes the caster's hands to get very very hot.  The caster can then direct the heat to one target, causing the target some physical damage.
#0
